# Bottom Navigation Layout Rules

Locked files: `src/components/BottomNav.tsx` and `src/components/bottom-nav.module.css`, rendered once as a **direct child of `<body>`** in `src/app/layout.tsx`. Do not add a second nav in pages.

- Do NOT `position: fixed` on `html`. Do NOT make `body` a flex column or `overflow-y: auto`.
- Geometry in `bottom-nav.module.css`: `.fixedNav` is `bottom: 0`, `height: 52px`, `padding-bottom: 0`, `margin-bottom: 0`. Safe-area inset lives on `.navInner` as `padding-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px)` with `box-sizing: content-box` so the bar fills the glass and icons stay above the home indicator. Do not add Tailwind `pb-*` / `mb-*` / `pb-safe` on the nav.
- Do NOT hide the nav on route change.

Every route uses `PageShell` with `w-full min-h-full pb-[calc(60px+env(safe-area-inset-bottom))] pt-[env(safe-area-inset-top)] bg-background`.
`PageHeader` is not sticky.
